# Wave W17-AD (Amber Sea — West): wake rock — a low rounded wake-washed boulder standing in the shipped sea, its crown washed pale by every crossing’s wash, foam collar at its base (design: small rocky islets in the lane). West’s own rock — split from Central’s taller garden rock by stance entire (low and wash-rounded vs tall and bright-faced) and from Maris’s mooring rock by wear: this stone is smoothed by traffic, that one is rope-worn.
